guide: decapitator:
{
  "plugin": "Decapitator (Soundtoys)",
  "overview": "Soundtoys' analog saturator. Five Styles model hardware: A (Ampex 350 tape preamp), E (EMI/Chandler TG channel), N (Neve 1057 input), T and P (Thermionic Culture Vulture, triode and pentode). Drive pushes the circuit; Low Cut and High Cut shape it (Thump adds a bump at the low cut, Steep steepens the high cut); Tone tilts dark to bright; Punish adds 20 dB of drive; Mix blends in the dry; Output sets the level, and Auto ties it to Drive. Small: every control is a parameter.",
  "canTurn": [
    {
      "name": "Knob 1",
      "ref": "7:parameter:1",
      "now": "812 Hz"
    }
  ],
  "parameters": {
    "total": 7,
    "canTurn": 1,
    "notConfigured": 6,
    "groups": [
      {
        "group": "Knob",
        "count": 1,
        "names": [
          "Knob 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Out",
        "count": 1,
        "names": [
          "Out Gain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "A",
        "count": 2,
        "names": [
          "A Level",
          "A Pan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "LFO 1",
        "count": 2,
        "names": [
          "LFO 1 Rate",
          "LFO 1 Depth"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Controls",
      "about": "As on its face.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "role": "drive",
          "about": "0–10: how hard the circuit is pushed.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "style",
          "about": "A full and smooth, E bright and crisp, N thick in the mids, T and P aggressive (P the most).",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "filters",
          "about": "Hz: what's cut from the lows and the top.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "filter switches",
          "about": "Thump: a resonant bump at the low cut. Steep: a steeper high cut.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "tone",
          "about": "Dark to bright; the center is neutral.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "punish",
          "about": "On: 20 dB more drive, for destruction.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "mix",
          "about": "Dry/wet, 0–100%: parallel saturation in place.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "output",
          "about": "Output in dB; Auto lowers it as Drive rises, for fair comparisons.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recipes": [
    {
      "name": "Drum bus smash",
      "how": "Style N or E, Drive 6–8, Mix 25–35%, High Cut 10 kHz; Punish on for more. Auto on to judge it fairly."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bass growl, clean sub",
      "how": "Style T or P, Drive 4–6, Low Cut 80–120 Hz with Thump, Tone a little bright, Mix 40–60%: the dry keeps the sub, the wet growls."
    },
    {
      "name": "Vocal grit",
      "how": "Style A, Drive 3–5, High Cut 8–10 kHz with Steep, Mix 30–40%, Auto on."
    },
    {
      "name": "Synth warmth",
      "how": "Style A or N, Drive 2–3, Mix 100%, Tone a step toward dark."
    },
    {
      "name": "Telephone",
      "how": "Style E, Drive 7, Low Cut 400 Hz, High Cut 3 kHz with Steep, Punish on, Mix 100%."
    }
  ],
  "beyond": "Every control is a parameter; presets are in its window's preset menu.",
  "byRole": "tune takes a role from these sections in knobs (such as \"ceiling\"), or a job (\"limiter gain\", \"ceiling\", \"eq gain\"): Kumi finds its knob among the plug-in's names in Live and turns it only when it's configured, saying which to configure when it isn't.",
  "toTurnMore": "Live lets Kumi turn only the parameters configured in the device. To add some: the producer clicks Configure in the plug-in's title bar and moves those knobs in its window once (Live keeps them with the Set; Save as Default Configuration in the title bar's menu keeps them for every new one). Kumi can open the plug-in's window with set_device_details (isEditorOpen)."
}

guide: ott:
{
  "plugin": "OTT (Xfer Records)",
  "overview": "Xfer's free three-band compressor, after the OTT preset of Live's Multiband Dynamics. Each band (high, mid, low) is pushed down above one threshold and pulled up below another, so detail and tails come up and peaks come down: dense, bright, loud. Depth blends the whole effect, Time scales attack and release, In and Out Gain set the levels, and each band has an output gain.",
  "canTurn": [
    {
      "name": "Knob 1",
      "ref": "7:parameter:1",
      "now": "812 Hz"
    }
  ],
  "parameters": {
    "total": 7,
    "canTurn": 1,
    "notConfigured": 6,
    "groups": [
      {
        "group": "Knob",
        "count": 1,
        "names": [
          "Knob 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Out",
        "count": 1,
        "names": [
          "Out Gain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "A",
        "count": 2,
        "names": [
          "A Level",
          "A Pan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "LFO 1",
        "count": 2,
        "names": [
          "LFO 1 Rate",
          "LFO 1 Depth"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Controls",
      "about": "Its knobs and sliders.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "role": "depth",
          "about": "0–100%, the effect's dry/wet: 100% is full OTT, 20–40% the usual touch.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "time",
          "about": "Scales attack and release: lower is snappier and grittier, higher smoother.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "in gain",
          "about": "dB into the bands: more drives more compression.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "out gain",
          "about": "dB out: OTT gets loud, so level-match here.",
          "live": [
            "Out Gain"
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "upward",
          "about": "%: how far quiet parts are lifted; lower it to keep noise and tails down.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "downward",
          "about": "%: how far loud parts are pushed down.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "band gains",
          "about": "Each band's output, dB: tilt the tone (Low down if it muddies, High down if it hisses).",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recipes": [
    {
      "name": "A touch on a synth",
      "how": "Depth 20–35%, Time at its default or a little lower, Out Gain to match the bypassed level: movement and air without flattening it."
    },
    {
      "name": "Full squash for sound design",
      "how": "Depth 100%, In Gain +3 to +6 dB, Upward and Downward at full, Out Gain down 4–8 dB. An EQ or low cut after it: it lifts hiss, room and tails. Common on growls and resampled basses."
    },
    {
      "name": "Drums with air",
      "how": "Depth 15–25%, Upward 30–50% so tails don't swell, Downward full; the Low band down 1–3 dB if kicks bloom."
    },
    {
      "name": "Dense tails",
      "how": "After a reverb or delay, Depth 40–60%: tails come forward and shimmer. Watch the noise floor."
    }
  ],
  "beyond": "OTT is simple: its knobs and sliders are its parameters. What it lacks (crossover points, ratios, attack in ms) needs Live's Multiband Dynamics, where OTT is a preset.",
  "byRole": "tune takes a role from these sections in knobs (such as \"ceiling\"), or a job (\"limiter gain\", \"ceiling\", \"eq gain\"): Kumi finds its knob among the plug-in's names in Live and turns it only when it's configured, saying which to configure when it isn't.",
  "toTurnMore": "Live lets Kumi turn only the parameters configured in the device. To add some: the producer clicks Configure in the plug-in's title bar and moves those knobs in its window once (Live keeps them with the Set; Save as Default Configuration in the title bar's menu keeps them for every new one). Kumi can open the plug-in's window with set_device_details (isEditorOpen)."
}

guide: ozone12:
{
  "plugin": "Ozone 12 (iZotope)",
  "overview": "iZotope's mastering suite: one plug-in holding a chain of modules, processed in order. The core: Equalizer, Dynamic EQ, Dynamics (a multiband compressor), Imager, Exciter, and the Maximizer last. Also Low End Focus, Clarity, Stabilizer, Master Rebalance, Match EQ, the Vintage modules, and in 12 Stem EQ, Bass Control and Unlimiter (several need Advanced). Parameter names start with their module; a module's parameters do nothing while it isn't in the chain. Advanced also installs each module as its own plug-in (Ozone 12 Maximizer and so on), with the same controls. Hundreds of parameters, so Live turns only the configured ones.",
  "canTurn": [
    {
      "name": "Knob 1",
      "ref": "7:parameter:1",
      "now": "812 Hz"
    }
  ],
  "parameters": {
    "total": 7,
    "canTurn": 1,
    "notConfigured": 6,
    "groups": [
      {
        "group": "Knob",
        "count": 1,
        "names": [
          "Knob 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "Out",
        "count": 1,
        "names": [
          "Out Gain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "A",
        "count": 2,
        "names": [
          "A Level",
          "A Pan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "group": "LFO 1",
        "count": 2,
        "names": [
          "LFO 1 Rate",
          "LFO 1 Depth"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Maximizer",
      "about": "The final limiter: loudness and the peak ceiling.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "role": "threshold",
          "about": "dB into the limiter. Ozone 12 shows it as Input Gain: higher pushes harder, louder and more limited (as a Threshold, lower does). Output is made up.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "ceiling",
          "about": "The highest peak out, dB (Ozone 12's Output Level): -1.0 for streaming.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "character",
          "about": "0–10: low is fast and aggressive, high slower and smoother.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "mode",
          "about": "The IRC algorithm: later ones stay cleaner when pushed; Low Latency for live use.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "transients and width",
          "about": "Transient Emphasis keeps attacks, Upward Compress lifts quiet parts, Soft Clip shaves peaks before limiting, Stereo Independence lets left and right limit apart (wider, a less steady center).",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "true peak",
          "about": "On: also catches peaks between samples.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Equalizer and Dynamic EQ",
      "about": "Bands with frequency, gain, Q and shape. A Dynamic EQ band moves its gain only while its range is past the threshold.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "role": "eq gain",
          "about": "dB per band.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "eq frequency",
          "about": "Hz per band.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "eq q and shape",
          "about": "Q (higher is narrower) and shape (bell, shelf, cut).",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "dynamic eq",
          "about": "Threshold (dB), the gain it moves to past it, frequency, Q, timing; cut or boost.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dynamics, Imager, Exciter",
      "about": "Up to four bands each, split by crossovers.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "role": "dynamics",
          "about": "Per band, a compressor and a limiter (Comp and Lim in Ozone 12's names): threshold (dB), ratio, attack and release (ms), knee, makeup gain, mix.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "crossovers",
          "about": "Where bands split, Hz.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "width",
          "about": "Width per band, -100% (mono) to +100%; keep the lowest band at or under 0. Stereoize widens narrow parts; check mono.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "exciter",
          "about": "Per band: the saturation mode (warm, tape, tube, retro…), its amount, and Mix.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tone and balance",
      "about": "Modules that reshape the whole mix's tone or balance, and the chain's levels.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "role": "low end focus",
          "about": "Contrast up tightens and punches the lows; down smooths them.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "clarity and stabilizer",
          "about": "Clarity lifts masked detail; Stabilizer rides the tone toward a target as the song changes. A little goes far.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "master rebalance",
          "about": "Level of vocals, bass or drums inside the finished mix, dB.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "ozone 12 modules",
          "about": "Stem EQ: EQ one part (vocals, bass, drums…) inside the mix. Unlimiter: brings back transients a limiter crushed. Bass Control: tightens and focuses the lows.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        },
        {
          "role": "chain in and out",
          "about": "dB into and out of the whole chain.",
          "live": "not among this plug-in's names (look in the grouped list)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recipes": [
    {
      "name": "Streaming master",
      "how": "Maximizer last: Ceiling -1.0 dB, True Peak on, Character 3–5. Lower Threshold until the loudest part limits 2–4 dB. Aim for -14 to -9 LUFS integrated by genre: streaming turns louder masters down."
    },
    {
      "name": "Loud club master",
      "how": "Threshold for 4–6 dB of limiting, Character 1–3, some Transient Emphasis to keep punch, Soft Clip on, Ceiling -0.3 to -1.0 dB. Dynamics low band 2:1, attack 30 ms, release 100 ms to steady the bass. Imager's lowest band (under 120 Hz) toward -100%."
    },
    {
      "name": "Glue",
      "how": "Dynamics with bands linked: ratio 1.5–2:1, attack 20–30 ms, release 100–200 ms, 1–2 dB of reduction. Exciter in a tape mode at 10–20% mix."
    },
    {
      "name": "Harsh top, boomy bottom",
      "how": "Dynamic EQ band at 2.5–5 kHz, Q about 2, cutting up to 3 dB only when it gets loud. Equalizer low shelf -1 to -2 dB at 100–150 Hz, or Low End Focus contrast up for tighter lows."
    },
    {
      "name": "Toward a reference",
      "how": "Use vst3 guide and listen compare_to to measure the mix and reference at matched loudness. Build or edit an Ozone chain with the supported preset fields, load it through the DAW, then measure and listen again. Match EQ captures and Master Assistant remain optional interactive features."
    }
  ],
  "beyond": "Master Assistant is a button, not a parameter: in Ozone's window (Kumi can open it) the producer picks a target (streaming, CD, or a reference track), starts it, and plays the loudest 10–20 seconds; Ozone builds a chain and sets the Maximizer. Its result is parameters Kumi can then adjust (configure the new ones). For presets and module ordering, use Kumi's built-in vst3 catalog/create/edit tools first: the suite and standalone module classes have native writers. Loading reference tracks into Ozone itself and Match EQ captures still use its window.",
  "byRole": "tune takes a role from these sections in knobs (such as \"ceiling\"), or a job (\"limiter gain\", \"ceiling\", \"eq gain\"): Kumi finds its knob among the plug-in's names in Live and turns it only when it's configured, saying which to configure when it isn't.",
  "toTurnMore": "Live lets Kumi turn only the parameters configured in the device. To add some: the producer clicks Configure in the plug-in's title bar and moves those knobs in its window once (Live keeps them with the Set; Save as Default Configuration in the title bar's menu keeps them for every new one). Kumi can open the plug-in's window with set_device_details (isEditorOpen)."
}

guide: pigments:
{
  "plugin": "Pigments (Arturia)",
  "overview": "Arturia's polysynth. Two main engines, each Virtual Analog, Wavetable, Sample (with granular) or Harmonic (newer versions add types), plus a utility engine (noise and samples). The engines feed two filters (in series or parallel), then the amp and three FX buses (A, B and an aux send), up to three effects each. Modulation: envelopes (the first drives the amp), LFOs, function generators, random sources, combinators, macros and a sequencer/arpeggiator; drag a source onto a knob. Hundreds of parameters, so Live turns only the configured ones.",
