  "beyond": "Not host parameters: an oscillator's type and its table or sample (the menu above its display, the wavetable editor, or a file dropped on the display), warp mode, filter type, the mod matrix (which source moves what, how much, on which curve: the MATRIX page, or a source dragged onto a knob), LFO and envelope shapes, which FX are in the rack and their order (the FX page, drag to reorder), the arpeggiator and clip sequencer. First check vst3 catalog/inspect: Kumi can create a complete preset, edit known stored fields and add initialized Distortion slots, then load through the DAW. Use the window only for operations outside the supported format. A wavetable Kumi makes (2048-sample frames, up to 256, with Serum's \"clm \" chunk) loads when the producer drags the file (from Live's browser or its folder) onto an oscillator's display.",
